I started another random character on Monday the 13th, getting a chaotic
human barbarian.

Nothing very interesting happened before Sokoban, where I had two luck
penalties on the top level. First was an accidental movement of a boulder
before noticing that I hadn't yet moved another boulder out of the way. 
So I had to squeeze in to move the other boulder away.
Then, entering the zoo, I once zapped a wand of striking at the crowd,
breaking the mirror of a nymph. Well, I survived and picked up the Bag.

In the Mines, on level 6, I killed a gnome and a dwarf on the same square
and noticed that one of them had been carrying Grayswandir.
So, that became my main weapon for the rest of the game, even though it
blasted me every now and then when I wielded it after using the pick-axe.

Still in the Mines somewhere, I lost my polyselfless conduct by finding a
polymorph trap and becoming a baby silver dragon for a while. 
Also lost a dwarwish mithril coat and some good cloak.

On dungeon level 14 I was sitting on a throne and got prompted for
something to genocide. I decided that I didn't actually need any master
mind flayers in the game.

There were only three random altars in the game. One of them was on level
18, guarded by a lawful priest. The other two were neutral, on level 19,
and one of them guarded by a priest, again. I quickly converted the
non-attended one (at turn 22007), and received Cleaver there at turn
25529 but never wielded it.

I found the Medusa level (the version with Medusa herself in the middle of
the level) on dungeon level 22, which was earlier than I expected. 
I was still at exp level 13, had no reliable means of crossing the water
(just two or three potions of levitation), and no magic resistance. 
I decided to try my luck with the "hallelujah trick". 
Pick-axed a hole and found myself on a maze level.
Found the stairs up, blindfolded myself, and heard Medusa die when she
looked at my polished silver shield. Stupid bitch.
I broke the statue of Perseus and found a pair of boots inside. Good.
Went back down the stairs again, dropped Perseus's boots and everything
else I wanted to get uncursed, and zapped a wand of cancellation at the
pile. 

And down to the Castle I went, in search for magic resistance.
Luckily there were no other lichs but two plain brown ones.
I got dropped to the castle level through a hole, so I explored the West
part for a while looking for the stairs.. until I found them ONLY TWO
SQUARES FROM THE MOAT! Never seen the Castle stairs THERE before.
OK, I read a scroll of earth and built the tunnel in front of the
drawbridge like I usually do. Didn't need too much playing the bugle to
find out that the passtune was "cbbcb". They didn't use much imagination
this time..
Soon somebody zapped a wand of striking from the inside, so no more
drawbridge guillotine. Well, at least I had killed one lich and one
disenchanter with it.

I cleared the Castle rooms and took a wand from a chest that was in the
first tower I checked. No gray dragons guarding the treasures, but a nice
silver one that was kind enough to leave me scales. No unknown cloaks in
the treasuries either.. so I decided to enchant the gray dragon scales and
wish for a cloak of magic resistance. The wand was immediately empty after
wishing for the standard two blessed scrolls of charging. OK, I used one
of the scrolls on the wand and got the cloak of magicres at +3 as I asked.

Now I was ready for the quest. And finished it with no special events
written in the note file.

Down to Gehennom.
Valley on level 26, Asmodeus on 30, Juiblex on 31, Orcus on 36, ladder to
Vlad on 37, the top floor of the Wizard's house at 40 and thus the bottom
floor on 42, first fakewiz level on 46 (no portal), the other fakewiz with
the portal on 47, and the vibrating square already on 48, closer to the
stairs than I remember ever seeing before. The stairs were near the West
wall, and I felt the vibrations before I had advanced even a fourth of the
level width!
In this game I really didn't need to search for anything.

I went up to the altar at the Orcus town to check the buc-status of the
Candelabrum, then back down to the stairs on the vibra level and dropped
the Candelabrum and Bell next to the stairs.

Up to level 1 to drop the scrolls of gold detection that I had, some wands
of digging and some other stuff I didn't feel like carrying around before
the endgame. Down to the co-aligned altar on 19, emptied my wands of
create monster, wrote scrolls of enchant armor to get my ascension kit
armor to shape.

Down to the Wizard's tower. After clearing the moat on the top floor, I
first zapped a wand of digging to the inner wall, then a wand of death.
Then I just bashed a vampire lord to death, grabbed the Amulet and began
racing down to Sanctum.

On the vibrating square I realized I only had 5 candles. Never bought any
from the Mines, I was going to buy the rest just before the final run.
Somewhere I found 5 candles on the floor, but forgot to go and buy the
missing two ones. Well, I was not going to go back to the Mines now. 
I used a wish for the two.
Down to Sanctum. Wished for a ring of conflict to make sure, because I had
never seen one, but I don't remember if I ever actually wore it.
Didn't feel too uncomfortable, because there were so few priests down
there. I had to walk around the whole temple before finding the door in
the last wall. No trouble with the high priest, and I used the altar to
buc-identify the stuff I had picked up after Orcustown.
Then I quffed a cursed potion of gain level and got out of the Sanctum.
Another on the vibra level, because I ended up on the wrong side of the
stairs from Sanctum and felt too lazy to walk my way around it or make a
shortcut.. 

The mysterious force was extremely gentle this time:
45->45,45->45,42->43,j->j,29->29. One time it threw me one level down and
four times teleported elsewhere on the same level.
The Wizard wasn't too active either: he reappeared first on the Juiblex
level (well, there he also double troubled), and after that only on level
5, Earth and Water.

On the Earth level I counted my scrolls of gold detection: two.
OK, so I wrote two more and read one. I got the route dug to the portal
needing only two wands of digging. Dropped at least a dozen of them, and
some other stuff, before going to Air. I got swallowed by air elementals a
few times, and one of them got my Hp reduced to about 25 of 257, and then
I prayed to get it restored. The remaining elemental planes were quick to
pass.. 

I arrived to Astral slightly to the right from the center of the screen.
Put on my blindfold to see that Death was guarding the rightmost altar
and decided to go first to the middle one, guarded by Famine.
She went down with about two swings of the +7 Grayswandir and +2 elven
dagger, #twoweaponed. The rest of the crowd there provided little
resistance, and soon I found myself standing.. on.. SET'S HIGH ALTAR.
The game had gone exceptionally easily this far, so I started wondering..
With my first 3.4.1 ascension I brought an ice box to the demigod bar.
Why not do the same with my first 3.4.2 ascension, too! I might develop a
tradition of it.

So I reached out for the Castle wand and wished for one. It got dropped to
the floor. Oh, a dragon corpse inside. Well, let's try to wrest the last
charge out for another ice box. It took quite a while, and Famine came in
to look what was going on and I had to re-kill her a few times before
finally getting the last charge wrested out. And another ice box with a
heavy corpse.
OK, I still have another wand of wishing somewhere.. I emptied it too, but
ALL the ice boxes had heavy corpses inside. I ended up with what, 6 ice
boxes on the floor.

I could have just forgot the ice boxes and sacrifice the Amulet to Set but
no, I decided to strip myself naked leaving only the gauntlets of power
on, and drop the rest of the stuff to try if I could get one heavy corpse
out of the ice box. I COULD have tried it in wizard mode but no, I did it
in the real game. And no, I didn't get it done.
And guess what happened while I was naked?
Yes, Famine decided to wake up.
Even then I could have just picked up THE AMULET and sacrificed it,
ascending with a minimal inventory listing with Famine right beside me.
But no, something went into me that made me bash Famine with my gloved
hands a few times, letting her reduce me to about 5 Hp.
And then I decided to pray, thinking that it must be enough time since my
previous prayer on the Air level. If I only had taken a glance at my
notes, I would have seen it was 322 turns ago even though it felt a lot
longer with all that trying to zap the final charge. 
So it wasn't safe and Famine hit me again while Set was busy not helping
me. But she NEVER made me HUNGRY!

Funny, I would have expected to feel much more furious after such a death
because of a stupid ascension trick on my god's high altar, but I was only
a little bit annoyed and almost more amused than anything else. I guess I
just had enough time to stand there with the amulet knowing that I could
ascend by just offering it, so I felt almost like ascending. 
Well, maybe I'll manage to make my first actual 3.4.2 ascension in the
contest.. 

